## Summary

I executed the Founder Charter end-to-end for **Mise**, an AI-native web-design agency, building the company and shipping a complete client product.

**Process followed:**
1. **Strategy** (`strategy/company-strategy.md`) — mission, target market (small food/hospitality brands), fixed-price offering ($1,500 Launch Site), and 5-role org design. One competitor-pricing web search used.
2. **Profiles** (`team/profiles.md`) — 5 role profiles with exact system prompts and model tiers.
3. **Interview/hire** (`team/hiring-log.md`) — interviewed 5 candidates in parallel on cheapest eligible models; **all 5 passed on the first try** — no promotions needed (cost floor achieved). Hired: CTO, Head of Design, CMO (all qwen-cloud), Frontend Engineer (qwen3-coder, free), Content Writer (qwen-cloud).
4. **Product** (`product/site/`) — static cooking-brand site "Forge & Hearth": homepage, blog index, 3 real recipe posts (cookable content), shared responsive `styles.css`, verified working internal navigation across all 6 pages. Plus `product/demo.md` demo script.
5. **Brand + marketing** (`marketing/`) — dual-brand identity (agency + client) with hex palettes/typography/logo direction, and launch collateral (3 social posts, cold email, press blurb, hero copy).
6. **Close the loop** (`FOUNDER_REPORT.md`) — what was built, org chart with model justifications, spawn count, and lessons learned.

**Cost optimization:** Every role on its cheapest eligible model; frontend on the free code model; zero mid-tier promotions. Shared brand/layout decisions coordinated via the blackboard. **10 total spawns** (5 interviews + 5 build dispatches), well under the 24 cap. I caught and fixed a "LeMond"→"Lemon" typo during review.
